.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-GET-ACCOUNT 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-get-account \- show one account's definition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eam get-account
.BR \-\-account | \-a
.I ACCOUNT_ID\fR|\fIERN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints one account as JSON: its account ID, its human-readable name, its
ERN, its description, and when it was created and last changed.
.PP
This is the same description
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-accounts (1)
gives of each of its own, for a single account asked for by ID. They share
one representation on purpose, so that a field added to a listing is in
this too rather than the two drifting apart.
.PP
The caller must be authenticated as a global administrator (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1)),
as for every other way of reading who exists.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-account " " \fIACCOUNT_ID\fR|\fIERN\fR
The account. Required. An account is named by its ID rather than by its
name: the ID is what an ERN's fourth field carries and what every resource
in the installation is scoped by, while the name is descriptive and
addresses nothing. A full ERN is accepted too and names the same account;
see
.B NAMES AND ERNS
in
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The account is printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, no such account
exists, or the caller is not an authenticated global administrator. If the
failure was an expired or invalid session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the stored
credentials file is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
By account ID:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eam get-account --account 000000000000
.fi
.RE
.PP
By ERN, which names the same account:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eam get-account \\
    --account ern:eam:eu-central-1:000000000000::account:000000000000
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-accounts (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-account (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-account (1)
